.TITLE "pwd"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Prints the name of the current working directory. It displays the __absolute path__ from the root of the filesystem to your current location.

.DIV "TLDR"
**pwd**
Displays the full path of the current directory.
> 

**pwd -P**
Displays the physical path, resolving any symbolic links to their actual locations.
> __-P__ physical path flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Knowing your exact location with __pwd__ is essential before running commands that modify or delete files, especially when working with scripts or symbolic links.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:cd** **mac:ls**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/pwd.html__
